      "observations": [
        "Actual native and independently imported front/rear/top renders were inspected against the current Combat Craft Type1.5 and Surveillance Craft Type5 GLBs in the same studio. Slab sides,smaller edge radii and stepped roof blocks now repeat their orthogonal construction language;grading blade and twin-tower working layout remain functional proposal distinctions.",
        "The main slabs,towers and roof steps are grey. Blue-grey and pale alloy are confined to service insets,fascia and tool details,with a small warm-oxide marker. Five colour/ORM map medians match actual canonical atlas tile interiors within one byte. Both embedded canonical map arrays equal the atlas;current canonical material_tiles metadata supports the region assignments.",
        "Technical failures were counted and retained:Repair attempt1 had six unsupported slot-back inserts;Terraform attempt2 had duplicate grey material slots consolidated by glTF. Actual diagnostic GLB views and sanitized failure records remain linked. Terraform attempt3 passes after slot deduplication. Repair's second actual export uses shared author revision3 with embedded backings and deduplicated materials;revision2 was never exported for Repair after the earlier Terraform failure stopped that queue.",
        "Actual working poses at0/1/2/3seconds were inspected. The grading blade uses its rooted tilt pivot. Repair sliders extend before two separate clamp jaws close/release;the square service head has its own wrist. Native/import checks pass for physical support and matching animated surfaces at six sampled poses. No extra arbitrary articulation is added to fixed hulls.",
        "Wear remains sparse and materials remain opaque. User artistic acceptance,physical game scale,platform profiling and continuous swept clearance are pending. These are new proposal units awaiting mechanics;canonical models and gameplay/runtime catalogues are unchanged."
